01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Marty Supreme is a 2025 American sports comedy-drama film directed by
Josh Safdie who co-wrote it with Ronald Bronstein.

11
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
Timothée Chalamet stars in the title role, with Gwyneth Paltrow, Odessa A'zion, Kevin
O'Leary, Tyler Okonma, Abel Ferrara, and Fran Drescher in supporting roles.

12
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Set in the 1950s, the film is loosely based on
American table tennis player Marty Reisman.

13
01:21:15,000 --> 01:21:21,000
Safdie and co-writer Bronstein began developing the film in 2018 after Safdie was gifted a copy of Marty Reisman's
1974 memoir, The Money Player: The Confessions of America's Greatest Table Tennis Champion and Hustler.

14
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
Safdie met with Chalamet in 2018 and offered him the lead role.

15
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:51,000
Following a multi-year development period, the project was officially announced in July 2024; it
marks Safdie's first solo directorial effort since The Pleasure of Being Robbed (2008).

16
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
Marty Supreme premiered as a "secret screening" at the 2025 New York
Film Festival on October 6, 2025, followed by a U.S.

17
01:46:15,000 --> 01:46:21,000
theatrical release by A24 on December 25, where it received widespread acclaim.

18
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:36,000
The National Board of Review and the American Film Institute
named it one of the top ten films of the year.

19
01:58:45,000 --> 01:58:51,000
The film received nine nominations at the 98th Academy Awards, including Best
Picture, Best Director (Safdie) and Best Actor (Chalamet).

20
02:05:00,000 --> 02:05:06,000
It also earned three nominations at both the 83rd
Golden Globe Awards and 32nd Actor Awards.

21
02:11:15,000 --> 02:11:21,000
Chalamet won a Golden Globe Award and Critics' Choice Award for his performance.

22
02:17:30,000 --> 02:17:36,000
The film explores themes of new york city, london,
england, paris, france, cairo, capitalism.

23
02:23:45,000 --> 02:23:51,000
The tone is emotional.
